
"smart_sources:2024-08-27 - Digging at historic site in Boise unearths 150-year-old artifacts. What did they find_.md": {"path":"2024-08-27 - Digging at historic site in Boise unearths 150-year-old artifacts. What did they find_.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"1q9dzp4","at":1785795030090},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1785511728364,"size":12359,"at":1785795030154,"hash":"1q9dzp4"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,9],"#":[10,37],"###Assay Office history":[38,59],"###Assay Office history#{1}":[40,59],"###Making history real":[60,91],"###Making history real#{1}":[62,91],"###What’s next":[92,126],"###What’s next#{1}":[94,126]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Scott McIntosh","target":"Scott McIntosh","line":5},{"title":"Idaho","target":"Idaho","line":12},{"title":"Idaho State Historic Preservation Office","target":"https://history.idaho.gov/shpo/idaho-shpo-guidance/","line":22},{"title":"This photo shows the cross-section of soil where historical artifacts were found on the grounds of the Assay Office building in Boise. The red lines highlight the area where the artifacts were deposited.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/6pcfmz/picture291490220/alternates/FREE_1200/Dig%20site.jpg","line":24,"embedded":true},{"title":"One of the more interesting items among the artifacts unearthed at a construction site on the grounds of the Assay Office building in Boise is this Union General Service Button from around 1855-77 that might have been worn on a frock coat cuff or a cap.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/9g652o/picture291501795/alternates/FREE_1200/Union%20button.jpg","line":34,"embedded":true},{"title":"As I wrote in a column in May","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/opinion/from-the-opinion-editor/article288291170.html","line":40},{"title":"Among the items found at the construction site on the grounds of the Assay Office building in Boise were crucibles, including this one nearly intact. Crucibles were used to process and refine ore samples and were the largest of the containers found on the site.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/wod055/picture291538095/alternates/FREE_1200/IMG_0546.JPG","line":56,"embedded":true},{"title":"Idaho State Historic Preservation Office","target":"https://history.idaho.gov/shpo/","line":62},{"title":"The cupel, used in the process of purifying gold and silver, is still stained with the minerals, such as lead, copper, zinc or arsenic, that were leached out of ore in the purification process.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/kdcom5/picture291500795/alternates/FREE_1200/Cupel2.jpg","line":66,"embedded":true},{"title":"Dan Everhart, Idaho State Historic Preservation Office outreach historian, points to a maker’s mark on the base of a crucible, used to process and refine ore samples. Such maker’s marks allow historians to date the artifact based on when the company was in business.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/ce0qs2/picture291395880/alternates/FREE_1200/IMG_1990.jpg","line":78,"embedded":true},{"title":"Chris Shaver, archaeologist for the Idaho State Historic Preservation Office, holds some of the smaller items found at the construction site around the Assay Office building.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/aocgbx/picture291395810/alternates/FREE_1200/IMG_1998.jpg","line":88,"embedded":true},{"title":"![Profile Image of Scott McIntosh","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/32oljv/picture234187782/alternates/FREE_1200/0813mcintosh02%20Cropped.jpg","line":114},{"title":"208-377-6202","target":"tel:208-377-6202","line":120},{"title":"Support my work with a digital subscription","target":"https://mycheckout.idahostatesman.com/subscribe?ofrgp_id=394&g2i_or_o=Event&g2i_or_p=Reporter&cid=news_cta_0.99-1mo-15.99-on-article_202404","line":122}],"metadata":{"title":"Digging at historic site in Boise unearths 150-year-old artifacts. What did they find?","source":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/opinion/from-the-opinion-editor/article291395440.html#campaignName=boise_theidahoway_newsletter&linkType=nmeintro","author":["[[Scott McIntosh]]"],"published":"2024-08-27","created":"2026-07-31","description":"“I asked the crew to give me a call if they found anything. I was not expecting what we found.”","tags":["#idaho"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},